# The Flutter app is not part of the web deployment.
#
# Without this, `vercel deploy` walks mobile/build — 2.7 GB of Gradle
# intermediates and a 100 MB+ libflutter.so — and fails on the file size limit
# before it uploads anything. The serverless functions in api/ and the Vite
# build in src/ are the whole of what Vercel needs.
mobile/

# Server-side credentials. Vercel reads the service account from the
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT environment variable, never from a file in the
# bundle — a key inside a deployment is a key inside every function's disk.
service-account.json

# The admin panel is its own app with its own package.json, node_modules and
# build output, deployed separately. Walking it here uploads a second
# node_modules into this deployment for nothing.
admin/

# Build output of the browser extension — released on GitHub, not served here.
dist-extension/

# Local-only.
.env.local
scripts/

# NOT excluded, despite being a browser extension: api/sync.js imports
# extension/src/snapshotMapping.js so the server and the extension write
# byte-identical documents. Excluding it breaks the function build.

# Vitest suites for the functions. They sit next to the code they test (see
# vitest.config.ts), but Vercel treats every non-underscore .js in api/ as its
# own serverless function — the five *.test.js files pushed the deployment from
# 9 functions to 14, past the Hobby plan's limit of 12. Ignored here rather than
# moved so the tests stay beside their subjects and still run in CI.
api/**/*.test.js
